230 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 92 0 R/T(Addressing the Digital Gender Divide and Technology-Facilitated Gender-Based Violence)/E(Addressing the Digital Gender Divide and Technology-Facilitated Gender-Based Violence)/Pg 15 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

231 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 92 0 R/T(1.1. Introduction to the Agenda)/E(1.1. Introduction to the Agenda)/Pg 15 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

232 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 92 0 R/T(The digital gender divide)/E(The digital gender divide)/Pg 15 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

233 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 92 0 R/E(The divide should be understood as more than a connectivity statistic. A woman may technically have internet access while lacking a private device, affordable data, digital literacy, confidence, accessible content, a safe environment, or the ability to use technology independently. This distinction matters because policies that measure only subscriptions or coverage can report progress while leaving the underlying inequality largely unchanged.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

234 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 92 0 R/E(The divide is also shaped by location and social position. Rural women may face weak infrastructure; low-income women may ration data; women with disabilities may encounter inaccessible interfaces; and women living under restrictive social conditions may technically have connectivity while facing family or community restrictions on its use. A strong analysis therefore asks not simply who is connected, but who can use digital tools meaningfully, safely and autonomously.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

235 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 92 0 R/E(The digital gender divide is not one gap. It includes whether a person can obtain a device, afford connectivity, access electricity, possess relevant skills, use services safely, understand privacy controls, participate in digital economies and have meaningful opportunities to shape technology. A woman may technically be \215online\216 while still being digitally excluded through cost, poor quality access, social restrictions or harassment.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

