253 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 93 0 R/T(Technology-facilitated gender-based violence)/E(Technology-facilitated gender-based violence)/Pg 16 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

254 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 93 0 R/E(UN Women describes technology-facilitated violence as harmful acts committed, assisted, aggravated or amplified through digital tools, producing or potentially producing physical, sexual, psychological, social, political or economic harm. It can also occur offline through technology, such as GPS-enabled surveillance.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

255 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 93 0 R/E(Forms of TFGBV & the Technology Behind Them)/Pg 16 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

256 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 93 0 R/E(A spectrum rather than isolated incidents)/Pg 16 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

257 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 93 0 R/E(TFGBV can range from repeated unwanted messages to coordinated campaigns involving many accounts, manipulated media, financial abuse and offline threats. The same victim may experience several forms simultaneously.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

258 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 93 0 R/E(\200 Harassment and threats: repeated insults, sexualized abuse, threats of rape or physical harm.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

259 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 93 0 R/E(\200 Doxing and exposure: publishing addresses, phone numbers, workplaces or family information.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

260 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 93 0 R/E(\200 Impersonation: fake accounts, fraudulent profiles or identity misuse.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

261 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 93 0 R/E(\200 Non-consensual intimate imagery: real or synthetic sexual content distributed without consent.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

262 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 93 0 R/E(\200 Deepfakes and synthetic sexual content: AI lowers the cost of creating realistic fake media.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[18]>>
