endobj

359 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 97 0 R/T(International Frameworks)/E(International Frameworks)/Pg 20 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

360 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 97 0 R/T(CEDAW)/E(CEDAW)/Pg 20 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

361 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 97 0 R/E(CEDAW provides the broader human-rights foundation for examining discrimination against women, including discrimination that is reproduced through institutions, social practices and unequal access to opportunities. Although CEDAW predates the modern internet, its principles can be applied to contemporary forms of inequality when digital systems affect women\220s access to education, employment, public participation, services or justice.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

362 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 97 0 R/E(For this agenda, the important conceptual point is that digital policy should not be treated as gender-neutral simply because the technology itself is neutral in design. If women experience systematically different barriers or harms, States can examine whether existing equality and non-discrimination obligations are being effectively implemented in the digital environment.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

363 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 97 0 R/T(The Beijing Platform for Action)/E(The Beijing Platform for Action)/Pg 20 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

364 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 97 0 R/E(The digital agenda has subsequently required those principles to be translated into new contexts: who has access to digital information, who controls technology, whose voices are amplified or silenced, how women are represented online, and what remedies exist when technology is weaponized against them. The Beijing Platform is especially relevant to violence against women, education and training, women and the media, human rights and institutional mechanisms.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

365 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/P 97 0 R/T(2030 Agenda)/E(2030 Agenda)/Pg 20 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

366 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 97 0 R/E(The 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development, adopted by the General Assembly in September 2015, embeds gender equality across several interlinked goals rather than treating it as a single silo.)/Pg 20 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

