endobj

417 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 99 0 R/T(A resolution on this agenda is judged not by how much sympathy it expresses but by how faithfully it operationalizes a small set of recurring principles drawn from CEDAW, the Beijing Platform, the Global Digital Compact and UN Women's own guidance. Six principles should anchor every clause.)/E(A resolution on this agenda is judged not by how much sympathy it expresses but by how faithfully it operationalizes a small set of recurring principles drawn from CEDAW, the Beijing Platform, the Global Digital Compact and UN Women's own guidance. Six principles should anchor every clause.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

418 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 99 0 R/T(Non-discrimination and substantive equality. CEDAW's central legal concept is that formally equal treatment is not enough; states must achieve equality of outcome, not merely equality of opportunity on paper. Applied to this agenda, this means a country cannot claim compliance simply because internet access is technically available to women \204 if women systematically cannot use it safely, affordably or independently, substantive equality has not been achieved.)/E(Non-discrimination and substantive equality. CEDAW's central legal concept is that formally equal treatment is not enough; states must achieve equality of outcome, not merely equality of opportunity on paper. Applied to this agenda, this means a country cannot claim compliance simply because internet access is technically available to women \204 if women systematically cannot use it safely, affordably or independently, substantive equality has not been achieved.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

419 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 99 0 R/T(The continuum of violence. General Recommendation No. 35 rejects the idea that "online" and "offline" violence are separate categories requiring separate policy logics. Instead, it frames technology-facilitated abuse as an extension of the same continuum of violence that occurs in the home, the workplace and public life. This matters for drafting: a resolution that treats cyberstalking as unrelated to intimate-partner violence, for instance, will miss that the same coercive-control dynamic often operates through both channels simultaneously.)/E(The continuum of violence. General Recommendation No. 35 rejects the idea that "online" and "offline" violence are separate categories requiring separate policy logics. Instead, it frames technology-facilitated abuse as an extension of the same continuum of violence that occurs in the home, the workplace and public life. This matters for drafting: a resolution that treats cyberstalking as unrelated to intimate-partner violence, for instance, will miss that the same coercive-control dynamic often operates through both channels simultaneously.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

420 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 99 0 R/T(Survivor-centred response. A reporting mechanism is not successful merely because it exists or receives complaints. The relevant test is whether survivors can safely report, understand the process, obtain timely and meaningful remedies, and avoid retaliation or re-traumatization. This principle should discipline any clause that proposes a "hotline," "reporting portal," or "grievance mechanism" \204 the existence of the mechanism is not the outcome; the survivor's actual experience of it is.)/E(Survivor-centred response. A reporting mechanism is not successful merely because it exists or receives complaints. The relevant test is whether survivors can safely report, understand the process, obtain timely and meaningful remedies, and avoid retaliation or re-traumatization. This principle should discipline any clause that proposes a "hotline," "reporting portal," or "grievance mechanism" \204 the existence of the mechanism is not the outcome; the survivor's actual experience of it is.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

