509 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 103 0 R/T(Jurisdictional fragmentation adds another layer. A single incident of technology-facilitated abuse can span a perpetrator, victim, platform and payment processor in different legal systems, while the Global Digital Compact's trust-and-safety provisions remain aspirational rather than binding. Enforcement currently depends on uneven national legislation \204 the EU's Digital Services Act, the UK's and Australia's Online Safety Acts, and India's IT Intermediary Guidelines are the most developed examples, but most states have no comparable framework.)/E(Jurisdictional fragmentation adds another layer. A single incident of technology-facilitated abuse can span a perpetrator, victim, platform and payment processor in different legal systems, while the Global Digital Compact's trust-and-safety provisions remain aspirational rather than binding. Enforcement currently depends on uneven national legislation \204 the EU's Digital Services Act, the UK's and Australia's Online Safety Acts, and India's IT Intermediary Guidelines are the most developed examples, but most states have no comparable framework.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

510 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 103 0 R/E(Finally, generative AI is advancing faster than either platform moderation or policy drafting can keep pace with: sexualized deepfakes can be produced and distributed across borders almost instantly, meaning narrowly worded, technology-specific rules risk becoming obsolete before they are even implemented.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

511 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 103 0 R/T(1.8. The Way Forward: Proposed Measures and Recommendations)/E(1.8. The Way Forward: Proposed Measures and Recommendations)/Pg 26 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

512 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 103 0 R/T(The clearest current roadmap available to delegates is the Beijing+30 Action Agenda, launched by UN Women at CSW69 in March 2025 and built on national review input from 159 Member States. It organizes future action around six priorities \204 a digital revolution, freedom from poverty, zero violence, full and equal decision-making power, peace and security, and climate justice \204 underpinned by two cross-cutting foundations, financing and gender data, with adolescent girls and young women placed at the centre of implementation. This gives a resolution a ready-made, already-negotiated framework to build on rather than requiring an entirely new architecture.)/E(The clearest current roadmap available to delegates is the Beijing+30 Action Agenda, launched by UN Women at CSW69 in March 2025 and built on national review input from 159 Member States. It organizes future action around six priorities \204 a digital revolution, freedom from poverty, zero violence, full and equal decision-making power, peace and security, and climate justice \204 underpinned by two cross-cutting foundations, financing and gender data, with adolescent girls and young women placed at the centre of implementation. This gives a resolution a ready-made, already-negotiated framework to build on rather than requiring an entirely new architecture.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

513 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 103 0 R/T(UN Women's UNiTE campaign operationalized this in 2025 by making digital violence against women and girls its focus for the 16 Days of Activism, explicitly framing the issue as a shared responsibility across governments, platforms, UN entities and funders rather than any single actor's task.)/E(UN Women's UNiTE campaign operationalized this in 2025 by making digital violence against women and girls its focus for the 16 Days of Activism, explicitly framing the issue as a shared responsibility across governments, platforms, UN entities and funders rather than any single actor's task.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

