941 0 obj
<</Title(The variation among these frameworks is itself instructive for delegates: some rely on statutory duties of care enforced by a dedicated regulator \(UK, Australia\), others on horizontal due-diligence obligations applied across a whole trading bloc \(EU\), and others on intermediary-liability rules tied to an existing IT statute \(India\). A resolution does not need to endorse any single model, but citing more than one shows the committee that platform accountability is achievable through several different legal architectures, which strengthens the case that a proposed mechanism is realistic rather than aspirational.)/Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Parent 936 0 R/Prev 949 0 R>>
endobj

