<</Title(mun@umt.edu.pk)/Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Parent 953 0 R/Next 962 0 R>>
endobj

962 0 obj
<</Title(umt_mun)/Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Parent 953 0 R/Prev 961 0 R/First 971 0 R/Last 971 0 R/Count -1>>
endobj

963 0 obj
<</Title(UN Women's UNiTE campaign operationalized this in 2025 by making digital violence against women and girls its focus for the 16 Days of Activism, explicitly framing the issue as a shared responsibility across governments, platforms, UN entities and funders rather than any single actor's task.)/Dest[26 0 R/Fit]/Parent 943 0 R/Prev 954 0 R/Next 972 0 R>>
endobj

964 0 obj
<</Title(umt_mun)/Dest[26 0 R/Fit]/Parent 943 0 R/Prev 972 0 R/Next 955 0 R>>
endobj

965 0 obj
<</Title(he normative frameworks above set out rights and principles; the following national and regional platform-accountability laws show how several States have already begun translating those principles into enforceable rules that touch directly on technology-facilitated violence against women. Delegates can cite these as existing precedents rather than asking the Council to invent regulatory concepts from nothing.)/Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Parent 936 0 R/Prev 957 0 R/Next 973 0 R>>
endobj

966 0 obj
<</Title(\200 United Kingdom: the Online Safety Act 2023 received royal assent on 26 October 2023 and is being brought into force in phases by Ofcom, with illegal-content and child-safety duties enforceable from early 2024; it creates statutory duties of care covering harassment and intimate-image abuse.)/Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Parent 936 0 R/Prev 973 0 R/Next 958 0 R>>
endobj

967 0 obj
<</Title(Non-discrimination and substantive equality. CEDAW's central legal concept is that formally equal treatment is not enough; states must achieve equality of outcome, not merely equality of opportunity on paper. Applied to this agenda, this means a country cannot claim compliance simply because internet access is technically available to women \204 if women systematically cannot use it safely, affordably or independently, substantive equality has not been achieved.)/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 959 0 R/Next 974 0 R>>
endobj

968 0 obj
<</Title(I)/Dest[23 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 975 0 R/First 976 0 R/Last 977 0 R/Count -2/Next 960 0 R>>
endobj

969 0 obj
<</Title(Case Study 1 \204 Women in public life)/Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Parent 960 0 R/Next 978 0 R>>
endobj

970 0 obj
<</Title(Intersectionality)/Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Parent 960 0 R/Prev 979 0 R/First 980 0 R/Last 981 0 R/Count -2>>
endobj

971 0 obj
<</Title(Jurisdictional fragmentation adds another layer. A single incident of technology-facilitated abuse can span a perpetrator, victim, platform and payment processor in different legal systems, while the Global Digital Compact's trust-and-safety provisions remain aspirational rather than binding. Enforcement currently depends on uneven national legislation \204 the EU's Digital Services Act, the UK's and Australia's Online Safety Acts, and India's IT Intermediary Guidelines are the most developed examples, but most states have no comparable framework.)/Dest[26 0 R/Fit]/Parent 962 0 R>>
endobj

972 0 obj
<</Title(mun@umt.edu.pk)/Dest[26 0 R/Fit]/Parent 943 0 R/Prev 963 0 R/Next 964 0 R>>
endobj

973 0 obj
<</Title(\200 European Union: the Digital Services Act entered into force on 16 November 2022 and became directly applicable across all EU member states from 17 February 2024, imposing risk-assessment, due-diligence and transparency obligations on large platforms, including obligations relevant to gender-based online abuse.)/Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Parent 936 0 R/Prev 965 0 R/Next 966 0 R>>
endobj

974 0 obj
<</Title(The continuum of violence. General Recommendation No. 35 rejects the idea that "online" and "offline" violence are separate categories requiring separate policy logics. Instead, it frames technology-facilitated abuse as an extension of the same continuum of violence that occurs in the home, the workplace and public life. This matters for drafting: a resolution that treats cyberstalking as unrelated to intimate-partner violence, for instance, will miss that the same coercive-control dynamic often operates through both channels simultaneously.)/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 967 0 R/Next 975 0 R>>
endobj

975 0 obj
<</Title(Survivor-centred response. A reporting mechanism is not successful merely because it exists or receives complaints. The relevant test is whether survivors can safely report, understand the process, obtain timely and meaningful remedies, and avoid retaliation or re-traumatization. This principle should discipline any clause that proposes a "hotline," "reporting portal," or "grievance mechanism" \204 the existence of the mechanism is not the outcome; the survivor's actual experience of it is.)/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 974 0 R/Next 968 0 R>>
endobj

